651-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
652-# #524 (armbdt): block data transfer through a COLD host page.
653-#
654-# arm_pop()/arm_push() take a fast path when the host page is resident and a
655-# slow memory_rw() path when it is not.  The fast path truncates the low two
656-# address bits for free; the slow path passed the RAW address, whose transfer
657-# is a page-granular memcpy -- so an unaligned base SPLICED BYTES ACROSS A WORD
658-# BOUNDARY and the same instruction returned different bytes according to host
659-# page-cache warmth.  Fixed by masking AT THE TWO ACCESS SITES ONLY; the mask
660-# must never move to function entry, because writeback uses the unmasked
661-# running address.
